{"duration_api_ms":295331,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"a8a0d17e-c7fc-4c84-ab3d-b3a99f580555","total_cost_usd":1.4415471999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":129454,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":1635456,"output_tokens":29832,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"deepseek-v4-pro[1m]":{"inputTokens":129454,"outputTokens":29832,"cacheReadInputTokens":1635456,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.4415471999999998,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"deepseek-v4-pro[1m]","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"unknown"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"call_01_Z8RnQZkqKLJVxl5sosUy4170","tool_input":{"command":"which ai-sdd; ai-sdd --help 2>&1 | head -40","description":"Locate ai-sdd CLI and help"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"call_01_SwGBEi8yfge9SYkCvDD49557","tool_input":{"command":"ls ~/.claude/plugins/ 2>/dev/null; find ~/.claude -maxdepth 4 -name \"*.js\" -path \"*ai-sdd*\" 2>/dev/null | head -5; find ~/.claude -maxdepth 5 -type d -name \"*ai-sdd*\" 2>/dev/null | head -5; npm ls -g 2>/dev/null | grep -i sdd; pipx list 2>/dev/null | grep -i sdd","description":"Locate ai-sdd plugin or package installation"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"call_00_YIpM1e3Mt9Bbgbmcl8RG4921","tool_input":{"command":"ls ~/.claude/plugins/ 2>/dev/null; echo \"---\"; ls ~/.claude/plugins/*/ 2>/dev/null | head -40","description":"List Claude plugin directories"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"call_02_m6Yp21tYLZb1t3AetcpS6691","tool_input":{"command":"ai-sdd --help","description":"Show ai-sdd CLI help"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"call_00_KjLczPpIjDmOWh79U2Cd7568","tool_input":{"command":"grep -rn \"CNSaveRequest\" ios/ --include=\"*.swift\" | head -5; echo \"---exit:$?---\"; grep -n \"func save\\|func load\\|func delete\\|512\\|Application Support\\|ContactPhotos\\|throws\" ios/ElderlyAssistant/Services/Storage/ContactPhotoStore.swift | head -20","description":"Confirm no CNSaveRequest exists; ContactPhotoStore signatures"}},{"tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"call_00_QZFL6qn1uIcdkD0BgKTS5788","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/anjan/workspace/projects/elderly-ai-assistant-family-contacts-unify/specs/define-requirements/FR/FR-FCU-001-system-contact-link-storage.md","content":"# FR-FCU-001: System-contact link stored on the family contact\n\n## Metadata\n- **Area:** Link / Storage\n- **Priority:** MUST\n- **Source:** Feature constitution \"Link Identity & Dedupe Contract\" (binding properties 1, 4, 5) and \"Integration Surfaces\" (`FamilyContactStore.swift` — `FamilyContact` struct at :61, unversioned store); owner request 2026-10-12 (scaffold brief, ask 1: LINK); workflow `define-requirements` scope comment\n\n## Description\nA family contact **must** be able to carry a stored link to one system (Apple Contacts) contact, so the two records are ONE person and never two rows anywhere in the app. The binding properties:\n\n- **Stored on the family contact** — the link is a field on `FamilyContact`, following the house migration rule (optional field, custom-decoder default): a pre-link payload loads unlinked, and a corrupt/unknown link value must not fail the whole store read (the `try? decodeIfPresent ?? default` pattern of the existing decoder at `FamilyContactStore.swift:122–150`).\n- **One link at a time** — a family contact carries at most one system-contact link; re-linking to a different system contact replaces the old link atomically (no window where the contact is double-linked).\n- **The link identifies the system record** — it references the system contact's identifier (the shape — `CNContact.identifier` vs another key — is design-l1's to fix); the system record's name/number are NOT copied into the family contact by the link (the link is identity evidence, not a data copy).\n- **Explicit, never inferred** — a link exists only when the owner (or caregiver) created it through the link flow (FR-FCU-006); number similarity alone never creates a link.\n- **No change to emergency semantics** — linking/unlinking never alters `isEmergencyContact`, preferred-call apps, or the emergency dial order.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n```gherkin\nFeature: System-contact link storage\n\n  Scenario: A pre-link payload loads unlinked\n    Given a store payload written before the link field existed\n    When the store loads\n    Then the family contact loads with no link\n    And every other field keeps its pre-link value\n\n  Scenario: A linked contact persists its link across app restarts\n    Given a family contact linked to a system contact\n    When the app is restarted\n    Then the family contact still carries the same link\n\n  Scenario: A corrupt link value never fails the store read\n    Given a payload whose link field holds an unknown or malformed value\n    When the store loads\n    Then the family contact loads unlinked\n    And the rest of the store payload loads normally\n\n  Scenario: Re-linking replaces the old link atomically\n    Given a family contact linked to system contact A\n    When the owner links it to system contact B\n    Then the contact carries exactly one link, to B\n    And no state exists where the contact is linked to both A and B\n```\n\n## Related\n- FR: FR-FCU-006 (the link/unlink flow), FR-FCU-005 (stale-link degradation)\n- NFR: NFR-FCU-010 (migration compatibility), NFR-FCU-002 (identity integrity)\n- Depends on: —\n"}},{"tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"call_01_zSUOdmrqX5fc9tBAVS7x8462","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/anjan/workspace/projects/elderly-ai-assistant-family-contacts-unify/specs/define-requirements/FR/FR-FCU-002-link-aware-dedupe-unified-search.md","content":"# FR-FCU-002: Link-aware dedupe — a linked pair is one row for matched and unmatched queries\n\n## Metadata\n- **Area:** Link / Dedupe\n- **Priority:** MUST\n- **Source:** Feature constitution \"Link Identity & Dedupe Contract\" (binding properties 1–3) and \"Integration Surfaces\" (`UnifiedContactSearch.swift` — matched-only `dedupe(matchedFamily:in:)` at :269); owner request 2026-10-12 (ask 1: \"never two rows anywhere in the app\"); workflow `define-requirements` scope comment\n\n## Description\n`UnifiedContactSearch.dedupe` **must** become link-aware beyond today's matched-only normalized-number rule: an explicit link is identity evidence independent of number spelling. The binding properties:\n\n- **One row for the linked pair** — when a query matches EITHER side of a linked pair (the family contact's name/number/relationship OR the system contact's name/number), the person appears exactly once in the unified results — for matched AND unmatched queries alike.\n- **Findable by whatever matched** — the surviving row keeps the matched representation; a query that matched only the system-contact side must still find the person (through the link), never fall through to \"no results\" because the family side did not match.\n- **Both directions** — the link dedupes the book row when the family row matched (as today), AND dedupes/supersedes the family row when only the system-contact side matched (a linked pair where the query hit the system record must not surface the family record as an unrelated second row).\n- **Dedupe widens only through explicit linkage** — number-only matches do not become more aggressive (FR-FCU-003); a linked pair whose query matched neither side surfaces exactly as today.\n- **The dedupe contract is testable pure logic** — the link-aware rule lives in the same pure-static seam as today's `dedupe` (no I/O), so the scoped `UnifiedContactSearchTests` suite exercises it directly.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n```gherkin\nFeature: Link-aware dedupe in unified search\n\n  Scenario: Query matching only the family side yields one row\n    Given a family contact linked to a system contact with a different number spelling\n    When the query matches the family contact's name\n    Then exactly one row is returned for that person\n    And the book twin row is dropped\n\n  Scenario: Query matching only the system-contact side yields one row\n    Given a family contact linked to a system contact\n    When the query matches only the system contact's name\n    Then exactly one row is returned for that person\n    And the person is findable through what matched\n\n  Scenario: A linked pair never surfaces twice\n    Given a linked pair whose both sides match the same query\n    When the unified search runs\n    Then the person appears exactly once in the result set\n    And moreAvailable counts the deduped union, not the raw rows\n\n  Scenario: A link survives a mismatched number spelling\n    Given a linked pair whose family and system numbers differ in formatting\n    When a query matches either side by name\n    Then exactly one row is returned for that person\n    And dedupe does not require the numbers to normalize equal\n```\n\n## Related\n- FR: FR-FCU-003 (unlinked behaviour unchanged), FR-FCU-004 (honored everywhere), FR-FCU-005 (stale-link degradation)\n- NFR: NFR-FCU-002 (identity integrity)\n- Depends on: —\n"}},{"tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"call_00_iCrw1NYaHvTqHN4xidZC5862","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/anjan/workspace/projects/elderly-ai-assistant-family-contacts-unify/specs/define-requirements/FR/FR-FCU-001-system-contact-link-storage.md","content":"# FR-FCU-001: System-contact link stored on the family contact\n\n## Metadata\n- **Area:** Link / Storage\n- **Priority:** MUST\n- **Source:** Feature constitution \"Link Identity & Dedupe Contract\" (binding properties 1, 4, 5) and \"Integration Surfaces\" (`FamilyContactStore.swift` — `FamilyContact` struct at :61, unversioned store); owner request 2026-10-12 (scaffold