 the same link\n\n  Scenario: A corrupt link value never fails the store read\n    Given a payload whose link field holds an unknown or malformed value\n    When the store loads\n    Then the family contact loads unlinked\n    And the rest of the store payload loads normally\n\n  Scenario: Re-linking replaces the old link atomically\n    Given a family contact linked to system contact A\n    When the owner links it to system contact B\n    Then the contact carries exactly one link, to B\n    And no state exists where the contact is linked to both A and B\n```\n\n## Related\n- FR: FR-FCU-006 (the link/unlink flow), FR-FCU-005 (stale-link degradation)\n- NFR: NFR-FCU-010 (migration compatibility), NFR-FCU-002 (identity integrity)\n- Depends on: —\n"}},{"tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"call_01_LuO4FD6YmRApH5U45tLl3342","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/anjan/workspace/projects/elderly-ai-assistant-family-contacts-unify/specs/define-requirements/FR/FR-FCU-002-link-aware-dedupe-unified-search.md","content":"# FR-FCU-002: Link-aware dedupe — a linked pair is one row for matched and unmatched queries\n\n## Metadata\n- **Area:** Link / Dedupe\n- **Priority:** MUST\n- **Source:** Feature constitution \"Link Identity & Dedupe Contract\" (binding properties 1–3) and \"Integration Surfaces\" (`UnifiedContactSearch.swift` — matched-only `dedupe(matchedFamily:in:)` at :269); owner request 2026-10-12 (ask 1: \"never two rows anywhere in the app\"); workflow `define-requirements` scope comment\n\n## Description\n`UnifiedContactSearch.dedupe` **must** become link-aware beyond today's matched-only normalized-number rule: an explicit link is identity evidence independent of number spelling. The binding properties:\n\n- **One row for the linked pair** — when a query matches EITHER side of a linked pair (the family contact's name/number/relationship OR the system contact's name/number), the person appears exactly once in the unified results — for matched AND unmatched queries alike.\n